  results <- matrix(0.0, nrow = epochs, ncol = ncol(X) + 2L)
  colnames(results) <- c("epoch", "nllr", colnames(X))

  # Reuse your batching loop and subtract the nllr_grad() gradient.
  # Fill each row with the epoch, full-data nllr(), and parameters.

  return(results)
}
@
\end{minipage}

Run this function with batch sizes $n$ and 10 for full GD and mini-batch GD, respectively. Reuse these runs in the next task, and include a short extract of the returned matrix with the input settings in your report.

\emph{Check:} \verb|mark_my_assignment(tasks = "gradient_descent_reg")|
\item (2p) Try different learning parameters $\eta$ and $\lambda$. When does the algorithm converge or diverge? Visualize the epochs (x-axis) and the penalized loss $\text{NLL}_r$ evaluated on all observations (y-axis). Show at least one plot per algorithm that converges.
\end{enumerate}

